Camoufox: PublicKeyCredential.getClientCapabilities() answers for the claimed OS.

Stock Firefox fixes six of its capabilities at compile time by OS
(dom/webauthn/PublicKeyCredential.cpp): largeBlob, hybridTransport,
passkeyPlatformAuthenticator and userVerifyingPlatformAuthenticator are true on
Windows and macOS and false on Linux; credentialProtectionPolicy and
enforceCredentialProtectionPolicy are false on macOS only. A Linux build
claiming Windows therefore answered Linux's table. Measured (cfparity cross-os,
headed, 2026-10-30): stock Firefox 158.0.1 on win-i9 true for the four, Camoufox
Pro on Linux claiming that machine false. isUserVerifyingPlatformAuthenticator-
Available() already matches (false on both: it asks the platform at run time).

The values follow the caller's context's navigator.platform
(NavigatorManager::GetSpoofedOS), else the host's own.

